# Example 13 — NLopt CRS pure stochastic global (no internal local).
#
# `GN_CRS2_LM` (Controlled Random Search) keeps a population of points
# and mutates by reflecting through the centroid of M random members.
# Unlike DLIB:GFS it has NO internal local-refinement phase, so the
# entire MAXEVAL is spent broadly canvassing the box. Pair it with a
# downstream local optimiser (a separate run, or this same config
# wrapped in a PRESTAGE strategy — see example 07).
#
# When to pick this:
#   - You want a global search that does not "spend" its budget
#     converging to one local minimum.
#   - You will follow this with a local WARM refinement.
#
# INIT.SEED makes CRS's internal pop initialisation deterministic.

OPTIMIZER
  INIT
    SEED 1717
  ENDINIT
  STRATEGY
    TYPE PLAIN
    LIB NLOPT
    ALGO GN_CRS2_LM
    MAXEVAL 12
  ENDSTRATEGY
ENDOPTIMIZER

LOSS L2
FAILSCORE 1e16
PC_ERMSE 0 0.0001
PC_LAMMPS --script ../common/lammps/Ecoh.in --varloss Ecoh 8.10 800

OPTIM RCUT2B (1) 4.0 6.0
OPTIM SGRIDMB (1) 0.1 0.4

OUTPUT 1
BOUTPUT 1
